A delay forgets the count the call landed in:
a delay of zero arms a timer line for the count already reached, and every deadline comes a count early.
The timer fires every due timer line,
so an Irq armed on one has its deadline ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due
Witness: fuzz cores-timer-across

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ static int op_captable(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
  */
 static uint64_t delay_deadline(uint32_t us)
 {
-    return timer_now() + timer_us_counts(us) + 1;
+    return timer_now() + timer_us_counts(us);
 }
 
